Please note that this function primarily uses the NumPy library for handling the array calculations and expects data types that can be converted to float (for numeric calculations) or to tuple (for structural transformations). This function returns a tuple of divergences. This function also inserts NaN for the conditions where the second tuple's element is not lesser than the first tuple's corresponding element. For nested tuples, comparisons and computations will be executed recursively. If some elements aren't numeric, they will be replaced by the mean value within the tuple.

